{
  "$schema": "./node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",

  // ── AN ASSETS-ONLY WORKER, AND THE ONLY HOST ─────────────────────────────
  //
  // A.6 Half 2 was re-aimed at Cloudflare on 2026-09-22, with the previous
  // host kept as a spare that also built `main`. The spare is gone as of
  // 2026-09-26: it had quietly stopped building `main` and was
  // answering with an older bundle on a URL that still resolved, which is not
  // a spare but a second, stale answer to the same question. This file is now
  // the only deployment configuration in the repository. The reversal, the
  // stale build and the removal are all logged in apps/web/OPEN-QUESTIONS.md.
  //
  // This file and the Workers Builds settings in the Cloudflare dashboard
  // must not drift. The dashboard's build command is
  // `pnpm check && pnpm --filter web build` from the repo root, which is the
  // full gate — a host that builds differently is a second definition of
  // "done".
  "name": "musie",

  // Today, per the compatibility-date rule: a new project pins the date it
  // was created, and moving it later is a deliberate act with a test behind
  // it. https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/compatibility-dates/
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-22",

  "assets": {
    // Vite's output, from the repo root — Workers Builds runs at the root of
    // the workspace because `pnpm check` is a root script that reaches every
    // package, not just apps/web.
    "directory": "./apps/web/dist",

    // ── THE WHOLE REASON THIS FILE EXISTS ─────────────────────────────────
    //
    // router.tsx is a `createBrowserRouter`, so /diary, /about-you and
    // /session/:id/:step are real paths with no file behind them. Without
    // this, a deep link — or a refresh anywhere but `/` — is a 404 from the
    // CDN before React ever loads. It is the `/*` → `/index.html` 200 rewrite
    // that every SPA host needs, written out.
    //
    // Cloudflare makes it explicit rather than guessing from the presence of
    // index.html, which is the one behavioural difference from Pages and from
    // hosts that infer it: forget it and the SPA looks broken only on deep
    // links, which is precisely what A.6 Half 2 exists to test.
    "not_found_handling": "single-page-application"
  },

  // ── PUBLIC, DELIBERATELY, AND NOT FOR LONG ──────────────────────────────
  //
  // Both of these default to `true`, so writing them changes nothing today.
  // They are here because the DEFAULT is the wrong thing to rely on: the app
  // is on the open internet from the first green build, and
  // apps/web/OPEN-QUESTIONS.md argues the beta must be CLOSED — a
  // subscription-licensed Epidemic Sound master and a `[DE] `-prefixed
  // placeholder content set are the reason. So the exposure is a written
  // decision with a name on it rather than a setting nobody chose.
  //
  // Ben accepted it on 2026-09-22 against H.0b — the account gate — landing
  // the next day. The window is the point: when the gate ships, the argument
  // for these two lines expires with it. Flip them to false, or put
  // Cloudflare Access in front, and the beta is closed again.
  //
  // `preview_urls` is the sharper one. Since Wrangler v4.44.0 it follows
  // `workers_dev` rather than standing alone, so leaving it unwritten gives
  // EVERY non-production branch build its own public URL as well — which is
  // the exact surprise Cloudflare changed the default to prevent.
  //
  // Changing either in the dashboard alone does not hold: the next
  // `wrangler deploy` restores whatever this file says, and with Workers
  // Builds that is every push to `main`. This file is the switch.
  //
  // ── AND REOPENED, 2026-09-23, BECAUSE THE GATE NOW DOES THE CLOSING ──────
  // Both true again, and the argument changed rather than being dropped.
  //
  // When they went false there was nothing left to reach: no `routes` block and
  // no custom domain, so `wrangler deploy` succeeded and no URL answered. What
  // reopens them is the build variable. `VITE_REQUIRE_ACCOUNT=true` is set on
  // BOTH Workers Builds triggers, so a visitor to musie.lipinskib.workers.dev
  // meets the sign-in gate and gets no further without credentials somebody
  // handed them. An open URL no longer means an open app — the licensed master
  // and the placeholder content sit behind the gate, not behind obscurity.
  //
  // PREVIEWS ARE COVERED SEPARATELY, and that is the half that needed Access.
  // Production is one URL somebody chose to publish; previews are a URL per
  // branch, appearing on their own, which nobody is watching. So Cloudflare
  // Access sits in front of the preview deployments only — a self-hosted app on
  // a `preview_worker` destination against this Worker, allowing Cloudflare
  // account members. Attached to the WORKER rather than to a list of hostnames,
  // so it keeps covering previews as branches come and go.
  //
  // Access is deliberately NOT over production: it would make every tester
  // authenticate twice, once to Cloudflare and once to the app, and put their
  // addresses in an allowlist as well as in `auth.users`. Revisit when a custom
  // domain lands — by then the audience may not be twenty people whose accounts
  // were made by hand. docs/MUSIE-SETUP.md §5.
  //
  // ── THE WINDOW WAS CLOSED · 2026-09-22, ON BEN'S CALL ────────────────────
  // H.0b shipped, which is the condition the paragraph above set. The account
  // gate is live behind `VITE_REQUIRE_ACCOUNT`, so the licensing argument no
  // longer rests on nobody finding the URL.
  //
  // READ THIS BEFORE DEPLOYING. There is no `routes` block in this file and no
  // custom domain attached, so with both of these false the Worker has NO
  // HOSTNAME: `wrangler deploy` will succeed and nothing will be reachable, by
  // anyone, including whoever is trying to run the second-device test that H.0
  // and H.0b are both still waiting on. That is not a failure state to debug —
  // it is this setting working.
  //
  // So one of two things comes next, and the entry in
  // apps/web/OPEN-QUESTIONS.md names both: a custom domain, or Cloudflare
  // Access in front of these URLs with them flipped back to true. Access is
  // the better fit while the domain is parked until print day, because it does
  // not need the domain to exist.
  "workers_dev": true,
  "preview_urls": true

  // No `main` and no `binding` on purpose. There is no Worker script: every
  // dynamic thing musie does is a Supabase Edge Function (reveal-track,
  // realtime-token) called from the browser, and those stay on Supabase.
  // `binding` is only valid alongside `main`, so adding one without the
  // other is a config error rather than a no-op.
}
